From 15b2f8f9ec93f9cd5d6b640703a7600f1f07f0b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:29:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] temp/hexagonrpcd: fork to let the sensor DSP write its
 registry

The OnePlus 8 Pro (and probably other OnePlus/Oplus SM8250 devices)
only reports the accelerometer when the sensor DSP can write its
registry. hexagonrpcd 0.5.0 serves the registry read-only, and its
listener stops on the first unsupported request.

Add four patches (sent upstream separately):
- fetch listener input buffers larger than 256 bytes
- dispatch apps_std method IDs above 30
- hexagonfs: writable mapped directories
- new option -w DIR: serve persist/sensors/registry from a writable
  directory (fwrite, fsync, fremove, ftrunc, frename)

Without -w nothing changes for other devices.

Signed-off-by: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
